From 3b61e96504d6ffaf6b00405b9474271cca77870f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omp <omp@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:08:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/23] kernel32/kernelbase/ntdll/dnsapi: export the APIs the
 licensing and browser stacks probe for

A relay capture of AutoCAD's licensing/identity stack (plus Edge/WebView2) showed several
GetProcAddress lookups that fail only because Wine does not export the symbol that Windows provides:

  kernelbase!FlsGetValue2                       (57x, msedge_elf/msedgewebview2/msedge)
  kernel32!IsUserCetAvailableInEnvironment      (4x, msedge)
  kernel32!GetProcessUserModeExceptionPolicy    (1x, acad.exe)
  kernel32!SetProcessUserModeExceptionPolicy    (1x, acad.exe)
  ntdll!RtlAreLongPathsEnabled                  (1x, AcPal.dll)
  dnsapi!DnsIsZtEnabled                         (1x, msedge)

FlsGetValue2 behaves like FlsGetValue (the two policy entry points were `# @ stub` placeholders in
kernel32's spec, so they were not exported at all).  RtlAreLongPathsEnabled reports the
LongPathsEnabled registry policy as on Windows, and DnsIsZtEnabled /
IsUserCetAvailableInEnvironment report the feature as unavailable.

Verified with tools/expprobe under Wine: all six names resolve through GetProcAddress and
RtlAreLongPathsEnabled() returns FALSE (the documented value with the policy absent).
